# .dockerignore — controls what gets sent to the Docker build daemon (build context).
# Smaller context = faster builds + no secrets leaked into image layers.

# ── Dependencies ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Never copy host node_modules — the Dockerfile installs them fresh inside the image.
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*

# ── Environment / Secrets ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# .env must NEVER be baked into an image layer — pass via docker-compose env_file
# or Docker secrets at runtime.
.env
.env.*

# ── Version Control ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.git/
.gitignore

# ── Logs & Runtime Output ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
logs/
*.log
coverage/

# ── Tests ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Test files add ~100MB (mongodb-memory-server binary). Keep them out of prod.
src/tests/

# ── Documentation ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.md
LICENSE

# ── OS artifacts ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ── Docker compose files (not needed inside the image itself) ─────────────────
docker-compose*.yml
Dockerfile*
